<h3 class="h6 mt-4">B1. Registration and Your Information</h3>
<ol class="signup-terms-list" start="1">
  <li>You must provide accurate, complete, and up-to-date information during registration.</li>
  <li>You must provide your correct name, contact information, service category, skills, experience, and other information requested by the Platform.</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="h6 mt-4">B2. Accepted Jobs and Cancellations</h3>
<ol class="signup-terms-list" start="3">
  <li>Once a Provider accepts a job, they should make reasonable efforts to arrive at the agreed location and time.</li>
  <li>If a Provider cannot attend an accepted appointment, they should notify the Client and Platform as soon as reasonably possible.</li>
  <li>Repeated cancellations, no-shows, or unreasonable delays may result in suspension or termination of the Provider account.</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="h6 mt-4">B3. Pricing and Payments</h3>
<ol class="signup-terms-list" start="6">
  <li>Providers must provide accurate pricing information where the Platform requires it.</li>
  <li>Any additional charges should be clearly communicated to and agreed upon by the Client before the additional work is performed.</li>
  <li>Providers must not demand unauthorized or undisclosed charges from Clients.</li>
  <li>Payments will be handled according to the payment method and policies established by the Platform.</li>
  <li>The Platform may deduct applicable commissions, service fees, or other agreed charges from Provider payments.</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="h6 mt-4">B4. Conduct and Client Property</h3>
<ol class="signup-terms-list" start="11">
  <li>Providers must:
    <ul>
      <li>treat Clients respectfully and professionally;</li>
      <li>maintain appropriate behavior;</li>
      <li>respect Client privacy and property;</li>
      <li>avoid harassment;</li>
      <li>not use Client information for unauthorized purposes; and</li>
      <li>not request unnecessary personal information from Clients.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>Providers must take reasonable care to avoid damage to the Client's property. Any damage caused through negligence or improper conduct may be subject to investigation and responsibility under applicable law.</li>
  <li>Client information obtained through the Platform, including Client names, addresses, phone numbers, photos, and service details, must be used only for completing the requested service.</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="h6 mt-4">B5. Ratings and Reviews</h3>
<ol class="signup-terms-list" start="14">
  <li>Clients may rate and review Providers after a service.</li>
  <li>The Platform may investigate suspicious or fraudulent reviews.</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="h6 mt-4">B6. Suspension and Termination</h3>
<ol class="signup-terms-list" start="16">
  <li>The Platform may suspend, restrict, or terminate a Provider account if the Provider:
    <ul>
      <li>violates these Terms;</li>
      <li>provides false information;</li>
      <li>receives repeated serious complaints;</li>
      <li>engages in fraudulent or unlawful conduct;</li>
      <li>repeatedly cancels or fails to attend accepted jobs;</li>
      <li>misuses Client information; or</li>
      <li>creates a safety or security risk.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>
<h3 class="h6 mt-4">B7. Legal Compliance and the Platform's Role</h3>
<ol class="signup-terms-list" start="17">
  <li>Providers are responsible for complying with applicable laws, taxes, licenses, permits, insurance requirements, and professional requirements relating to their services.</li>
  <li>The Platform primarily connects Clients with Providers. Unless expressly stated otherwise, the Platform does not itself perform the maintenance, repair, tutoring, plumbing, electrical, or appliance services.</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="h6 mt-4">B8. Acceptance</h3>
<p class="mb-0">By registering as a Provider and selecting "I Agree", "Accept Terms &amp; Conditions", or an equivalent confirmation, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to these Provider Terms &amp; Conditions.</p>
